※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4665 LANG_CONSTANT_CALL_IMPURE

※ What is laid out in the image is worked out while compiling, so the function
※ an initializer `in ⎕static` calls has to be one whose answer depends on what
※ it is handed and nothing else.  One marked `@[impure]` may change, or read,
※ what the program holds while it runs, and is refused.

let std := ⎕import("std")

let calls: mut u8 = 0u8

@[impure]
fn counted() → ⸨u8⸩:
    calls ← calls + 1u8
    ⸨calls⸩

let seen: ⸨u8⸩ = counted() in ⎕static

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if seen⸨1u8⸩: 0u6 else: 1u6
